WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:02.310
- There's a tendency to think that

00:00:02.310 --> 00:00:05.900
paparazzi are invading people's privacy.

00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:06.980
Hiding in the bushes,

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:10.140
trying to get some scandalous photo.

00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:13.167
We're just out here, making a living,

00:00:13.167 --> 00:00:14.171
just like every other person.

00:00:14.171 --> 00:00:15.300
(indistinct chatter)
(cameras flashing)

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:16.853
- [Paparazzo] Work those legs, girl.

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:21.860
- Right now, I want to
get Victoria Beckham.

00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:24.980
She comes out just before nine o'clock.

00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:25.990
Hopefully, we beat her there.

00:00:25.990 --> 00:00:30.030
It usually takes me
only 20, 30 minutes tops

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:32.830
to get out the door from,
when the second I wake up.

00:00:32.830 --> 00:00:37.230
So, I live in New Jersey, which
is very close to the city.

00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:39.090
I absolutely love taking the ferry,

00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:41.300
it's the quickest commute that there is.

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:44.380
It's as picturesque a
commute as there can be.

00:00:44.380 --> 00:00:46.670
But at the same time, I'm in my zone.

00:00:46.670 --> 00:00:50.643
I'm reading all sorts of
articles from the day before.

00:00:50.643 --> 00:00:54.710
So, I went to NYU for photojournalism.

00:00:54.710 --> 00:00:59.140
One of the assignments that I
was given in photo class was

00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:01.400
go out and take a photo of somebody

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:03.330
that you don't know on the street.

00:01:03.330 --> 00:01:06.568
And I ended up getting
a photo of Taylor Swift.

00:01:06.568 --> 00:01:09.260
And it was printed in People Magazine.

00:01:09.260 --> 00:01:12.180
So instead of just handing in my homework,

00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:14.970
I handed the professor a People Magazine.

00:01:14.970 --> 00:01:18.010
So, I ended up dropping
out after my first semester

00:01:18.010 --> 00:01:22.015
and meeting up with Cesar
and we formed a team.

00:01:22.015 --> 00:01:23.954
- It's been five years now.

00:01:23.954 --> 00:01:27.250
Five years actually working together.

00:01:27.250 --> 00:01:29.150
We formed this group, 247 Paps.

00:01:32.054 --> 00:01:35.410
- The mobile office has Wi-Fi.

00:01:35.410 --> 00:01:38.160
It's our hiding spot, it's our vehicle,

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:40.100
it's everything that we need.

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:42.150
All of our work is done from
there throughout the day.

00:01:42.150 --> 00:01:43.650
So, right now we're gonna head

00:01:44.646 --> 00:01:45.816
over to Victoria Beckham's hotel.

00:01:45.816 --> 00:01:47.077
She's here for Fashion Week.

00:01:47.077 --> 00:01:49.270
Fashion Week is one of
the busiest weeks for us.

00:01:49.270 --> 00:01:50.660
Hopefully, we make it there in time.

00:01:50.660 --> 00:01:51.780
I'm running a little bit late.

00:01:51.780 --> 00:01:54.760
She's been clocked at nine o'clock

00:01:54.760 --> 00:01:57.200
every morning for the past four days.

00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:58.823
We got here at 8:45.

00:01:58.823 --> 00:01:59.817
- [Cesar] Yeah.

00:01:59.817 --> 00:02:00.823
- Got everything all ready?

00:02:00.823 --> 00:02:01.656
- [Cesar] I took care of it.

00:02:01.656 --> 00:02:02.489
- Wow.

00:02:02.489 --> 00:02:03.880
So it looks like she's already out.

00:02:03.880 --> 00:02:07.154
The other photographers are
already editing their photos,

00:02:07.154 --> 00:02:09.550
which means she's long gone.

00:02:09.550 --> 00:02:10.440
Yeah, she gone.

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:12.830
We have a saying that
if it's meant for us,

00:02:12.830 --> 00:02:14.839
then we're gonna get it, so

00:02:14.839 --> 00:02:17.483
just brush it off, it's nothing serious.

00:02:18.950 --> 00:02:19.783
All right.

00:02:20.925 --> 00:02:22.404
- So we're going to
The Mercer to check out

00:02:22.404 --> 00:02:23.662
who is gonna be there.

00:02:23.662 --> 00:02:26.270
- So it's been a few hours,
we wanna get on the board.

00:02:26.270 --> 00:02:28.060
We haven't got any
photos yet this morning,

00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:30.310
so we kind of wanna go the easier route.

00:02:30.310 --> 00:02:33.510
We wanna sit by a hotel
where we know there's people.

00:02:33.510 --> 00:02:35.130
Kendall Jenner's staying here.

00:02:35.130 --> 00:02:36.693
Kaia Gerber's staying here.

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:46.200
We wanna sit here for a little bit

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:48.280
even though there's other photographers,

00:02:48.280 --> 00:02:50.233
which we usually tend to stay away from.

00:02:50.233 --> 00:02:51.902
I hate working around these guys.

00:02:51.902 --> 00:02:55.009
For every photographer
that shows up on a scene,

00:02:55.009 --> 00:02:57.520
the dollar amount gets sliced.

00:02:57.520 --> 00:03:00.530
They all are trying to get
the same exact shot we are.

00:03:00.530 --> 00:03:03.040
The real ideal situation
is to get something

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:04.250
that only you get.

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:05.970
Kendall Jenner, for example,

00:03:05.970 --> 00:03:08.910
an exclusive of her can be a few hundred

00:03:08.910 --> 00:03:10.650
up to maybe $1000.

00:03:10.650 --> 00:03:13.410
30 guys, 20 guys there,
taking the same photos,

00:03:13.410 --> 00:03:15.275
it's, you hope to make $50.

00:03:15.275 --> 00:03:16.630
We're gonna go get some coffee

00:03:16.630 --> 00:03:19.483
and move on to something
that's probably exclusive.

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:22.350
So we're driving around

00:03:22.350 --> 00:03:24.590
and we spotted some other paparazzi

00:03:24.590 --> 00:03:26.100
that were waiting in front of

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:29.330
one of the most popular
restaurants, Bar Pitti,

00:03:29.330 --> 00:03:32.180
so we had an idea that somebody was inside

00:03:32.180 --> 00:03:33.430
but we weren't sure who.

00:03:33.430 --> 00:03:38.360
- So it could be either Hailey,
Gigi Hadid, or Bella Hadid.

00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:41.973
- The other paparazzi were
scared off by us showing up.

00:03:44.619 --> 00:03:47.050
It turns out that it's Kaia Gerber,

00:03:47.050 --> 00:03:49.120
one of the biggest up and coming models,

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:51.029
daughter of Cindy Crawford.

00:03:51.029 --> 00:03:52.823
- [Cesar] Hey Kaia.

00:03:52.823 --> 00:03:54.693
How you enjoying fashion week, Kaia?

00:03:58.334 --> 00:03:59.167
- Since she's up and coming

00:03:59.167 --> 00:04:01.490
and she's wearing some great fashion,

00:04:01.490 --> 00:04:04.160
this could be a couple
hundred dollars, solid.

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:06.390
So our upload process includes

00:04:06.390 --> 00:04:09.243
picking which photos I
like best, quick crop,

00:04:09.243 --> 00:04:11.590
depending on the quality of the photo,

00:04:11.590 --> 00:04:15.480
we can make pennies or
we can make five figures.

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:17.844
- Kendall Jenner will be coming out,

00:04:17.844 --> 00:04:21.130
I say three minutes, four minutes tops?

00:04:21.130 --> 00:04:23.680
- We got a phone call
that Kendall Jenner's car

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:25.200
had just pulled up at The Mercer.

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:28.338
We're only five blocks away,
but in New York City traffic,

00:04:28.338 --> 00:04:30.710
that can be up to half an hour.

00:04:30.710 --> 00:04:32.653
- You guys might have to go by foot.

00:04:33.586 --> 00:04:35.554
- I guess we're gonna go for it.

00:04:35.554 --> 00:04:38.137
(upbeat music)

00:04:52.150 --> 00:04:54.027
Looks like we made it, so

00:04:56.692 --> 00:04:57.609
here we go.

00:04:59.397 --> 00:05:01.302
(all shout at Kendall)

00:05:01.302 --> 00:05:04.870
- [Paparazzo] Legs for days, Kendall.

00:05:04.870 --> 00:05:07.856
- So we arrived right
on time, got the shot.

00:05:07.856 --> 00:05:11.430
We gotta compete against all
the rest of those guys, so.

00:05:11.430 --> 00:05:12.774
This has gotta go online right away.

00:05:12.774 --> 00:05:13.607
- Who was it?

00:05:13.607 --> 00:05:15.720
- We're different from all
the other photographers.

00:05:15.720 --> 00:05:16.880
We work as a team.

00:05:16.880 --> 00:05:18.230
They're gonna all follow her, but

00:05:18.230 --> 00:05:19.450
we gotta send first.

00:05:19.450 --> 00:05:22.180
And it turns out we beat
all the other photographers

00:05:22.180 --> 00:05:23.627
to publication.

00:05:23.627 --> 00:05:25.823
- We're on a roll now.

00:05:28.630 --> 00:05:31.797
(all shout at Hailey)

00:05:37.780 --> 00:05:39.040
- So we got a tip from a restaurant

00:05:39.040 --> 00:05:41.213
that Bella Hadid had just came in.

00:05:45.090 --> 00:05:48.230
Generally, some of the
most popular clients

00:05:48.230 --> 00:05:51.630
that buy our stuff are
the Daily Mail, People.

00:05:51.630 --> 00:05:53.010
- [Cesar] Hey Bella.

00:05:53.010 --> 00:05:55.340
I'm so happy we caught
that stalker, Bella.

00:05:55.340 --> 00:05:56.370
For real.

00:05:56.370 --> 00:05:57.840
If you need us anytime, we're out here.

00:05:57.840 --> 00:05:59.210
- Thank you.

00:05:59.210 --> 00:06:00.738
- [Cesar] You're welcome.

00:06:00.738 --> 00:06:01.571
- Today's a good day, today's a good day.

00:06:01.571 --> 00:06:02.880
We're different from other people

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:06.530
because we value the
relationship and the longterm.

00:06:06.530 --> 00:06:08.900
We respect them, they respect us.

00:06:08.900 --> 00:06:10.458
Being the nice guys goes a long way.

00:06:10.458 --> 00:06:12.620
- Miles, this is me being you, okay?

00:06:12.620 --> 00:06:15.370
It feels amazing and I understand

00:06:15.370 --> 00:06:17.081
why you do what you do now,

00:06:17.081 --> 00:06:20.150
because I have to say,
it's quite invigorating.

00:06:20.150 --> 00:06:21.433
Ready, smile fuckers.

00:06:24.570 --> 00:06:27.520
- Ariana Grande's one of the celebrities

00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:30.920
that we have worked with
from the very beginning,

00:06:30.920 --> 00:06:34.060
before her career even began in music.

00:06:34.060 --> 00:06:35.810
We've had some great moments with her.

00:06:35.810 --> 00:06:38.950
One of the best stories was the day that

00:06:38.950 --> 00:06:41.680
Rihanna took me to the
club for my birthday.

00:06:41.680 --> 00:06:43.080
- [Announcer] But that's not Drake,

00:06:43.080 --> 00:06:45.900
that's Miles, her favorite paparazzo.

00:06:45.900 --> 00:06:47.560
- Cesar sent her a message

00:06:47.560 --> 00:06:49.880
letting her know that we were out there

00:06:49.880 --> 00:06:51.510
and that it was my birthday.

00:06:51.510 --> 00:06:54.610
So she came downstairs
wearing a huge red heart.

00:06:54.610 --> 00:06:58.047
She gave me a big hug, said
happy birthday and said,

00:06:58.047 --> 00:06:59.060
"I'm gonna meet you over

00:06:59.060 --> 00:07:00.970
at the club, you're coming with us."

00:07:00.970 --> 00:07:04.070
we walked inside together
and partied for hours.

00:07:04.070 --> 00:07:08.250
She bought me a very
expensive bottle of champaign.

00:07:08.250 --> 00:07:11.000
Just by being nice, we get some shots

00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:12.233
that nobody can get.

00:07:13.979 --> 00:07:16.330
Tiffany, Tiffany, can we
get a shot right here?

00:07:16.330 --> 00:07:17.797
- [Paparazzo] Over here, Tiffany.

00:07:17.797 --> 00:07:20.915
- [Miles] Paparazzi is a term that

00:07:20.915 --> 00:07:24.981
is endearing to me, I think
that it describes what we do.

00:07:24.981 --> 00:07:27.350
People look at paparazzi on the street

00:07:27.350 --> 00:07:29.158
and they automatically assume

00:07:29.158 --> 00:07:31.254
negative things about us.

00:07:31.254 --> 00:07:34.000
We're just out here making a living

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:35.540
just like every other person.

00:07:35.540 --> 00:07:38.600
We don't do anything
that's against the law.

00:07:38.600 --> 00:07:40.040
Most of the people that come to New York

00:07:40.040 --> 00:07:41.433
are doing press anyway.

00:07:43.080 --> 00:07:44.550
That's a wrap, man.

00:07:44.550 --> 00:07:46.920
- [Cesar] All right,
brother, take care, guys.

00:07:46.920 --> 00:07:47.753
- Pleasure, man.

00:07:49.520 --> 00:07:51.940
- [Interviewer] Can you talk to me about

00:07:51.940 --> 00:07:56.370
how much money you guys
are able to pull in a year?

00:07:56.370 --> 00:07:59.230
- It has to be more
specific than six figures?

00:07:59.230 --> 00:08:01.270
Let's talk about why
I'm uncomfortable first.

00:08:01.270 --> 00:08:04.600
We don't really like to
speak about what we make

00:08:04.600 --> 00:08:09.320
because it, it's different than

00:08:09.320 --> 00:08:11.460
what other people make in this industry.

00:08:11.460 --> 00:08:12.930
We've set our goal of trying to make

00:08:12.930 --> 00:08:14.610
a million dollars a year.

00:08:14.610 --> 00:08:17.050
And I think it's something that we're

00:08:17.050 --> 00:08:18.920
gonna achieve very soon.

00:08:18.920 --> 00:08:20.473
- Job well done, completed.

00:08:21.710 --> 00:08:22.640
- Good day.

00:08:22.640 --> 00:08:24.424
Time we got a little bit of sleep.

00:08:24.424 --> 00:08:26.074
And then start all over tomorrow.

00:08:27.431 --> 00:08:28.348
- Let's go.

00:08:32.172 --> 00:08:34.755
(gentle music)

